From the dataset: grav-ticon — TICON-3: tidal constants of 3,471 tide gauges from GESLA-3
  sea-level records (amplitude and Greenwich phase lag of 40 constituents) (data/grav/ticon/, every
  input with its own .explain)
Inputs:
- data/grav/ticon/raw/TICON_3.zip — download
Collected: 2026-11-14
Licence: CC-BY-4.0
Sources:
- M. G. Hart-Davis, D. Dettmering, F. Seitz, TICON-3: Tidal Constants based on GESLA-3 sea-level
  records from globally distributed tide gauges including gauge type information (data), PANGAEA
  (2022), doi:10.1594/PANGAEA.951610 <https://doi.pangaea.de/10.1594/PANGAEA.951610>
Evidence class (rule 10): check
Where the Earth's radius enters:
- frequencies and equilibrium arguments of the constituents: not the radius: each gauge's constants
  were fitted with the frequencies of the Moon's and Sun's motions; the page predicts the tide from
  them with the same arguments
What would vindicate the flat model (rule 5): Gauges whose constants show no twice-daily line at the
  Moon's frequency along a whole coast, or tides in small closed seas as large as on the open ocean,
  would favour a local Moon lifting water under itself.
