Notes: Four NOAA stations of the Great Lakes have rows with only one of the five numbers after the
  constituent name; they are skipped and counted. The gauge type 'Lake' also covers tidal lagoons
  and estuaries (M2 up to 3 m), so the page does not use it to stand for lakes.

